    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nTucked away in a private setting just off Church Street on Healy's Lane, this attractive three-bedroom detached home enjoys an enviable location in the heart of Skerries, within a short stroll of the town's beaches, harbour, schools, shops, cafés and restaurants.\n\nAn attractive stone façade gives the property plenty of kerb appeal, while private parking for two cars and dual side access add to its practicality. To the rear, a directly south-facing paved courtyard garden provides a wonderfully sunny, low-maintenance outdoor space.\n\nInside, the accommodation is exceptionally bright and spacious, with many rooms enjoying a dual aspect. A striking picture window extending over two floors floods the interior with natural light, while generous ceiling heights further enhance the sense of space throughout.\n\nThe entrance hall leads to a spacious kitchen/dining room with separate utility, opening through to the sitting room at the rear. French doors connect the living space with the south-facing courtyard, creating an easy flow between indoors and out. Underfloor heating features throughout the ground floor.\n\nA double bedroom and adjoining shower room on the ground floor offer excellent flexibility for guest accommodation, a home office or those seeking ground-floor living. Upstairs are two generously proportioned double bedrooms and a well-appointed family bathroom.\n\nFrom beautiful beaches and scenic coastal walks to a wide selection of shops, cafés, pubs, and restaurants, all amenities are within easy reach. Local attractions such as Skerries Mills and the Heritage Centre add to the area's charm, while a choice of schools, sports clubs, and sailing facilities make it ideal for families - offering the best of vibrant town-centre living.\n\nTransport links are excellent, with Skerries train station a short walk away, providing regular services to Dublin City Centre, as well as connections to Luas and DART services. The area is also well served by bus routes, including the 33/33X and Fingal Express to UCD."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.19m x 1.72m\nWith tiled flooring.\n\nKitchen / Dining area - \nWith tiled flooring, high ceilings, recessed lighting, fully fitted shaker style kitchen with floor and wall mounted cabinetry, wine rack, integrated dishwasher, double oven, hob & extractor fan and tiled splash back.\n\nLiving Room - 4.46m x 3.98m\nWith tiled flooring, recessed lighting, feature fireplace with gas fire and French doors opening to south facing rear garden.\n\nUtility Room - 1.79m x 1.73m\nWith tiled flooring, plumbed for washing machine, plenty of storage.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.17m x 4.14m\nWith tiled flooring, box bay window overlooking the lane.\n\nGuest Bathroom - 2.12m x 1.72m\nTiled floor to ceiling with W.C, W.H.B., Bidet and accessible shower.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - 1.53m x 2.95m\nWith wooden flooring, feature window from ground to first floor.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.46m x 3.99m\nWood flooring, feature window\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.46m x 3.39m\nGenerous double bedroom with wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.83m x 2.01m\nPart tiled wall to floor, with WC, WHB and bath with shower over.\n\nOutside - \nTo the front, there is a paved driveway providing off-street parking for two vehicles. Two convenient side entrances lead to the sunny, south-facing rear garden, which is laid out in a private courtyard style and features well-established flower beds with beautiful, mature planting, together with a garden shed.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Detached property in Prime town centre location.</li><li>Private off-street parking.</li><li>South facing rear garden. </li><li>Stone's throw from South Beach.</li><li>All amenities literally on your doorstep.</ul>"
      },
